er from a different index: decisive 0.6353 (n=3351); far_mamba 0.3508 (n=2748); far_rwkv 0.3415 (n=2952); far_gptneo 0.3926 (n=3105). F185's support was 3471.  THIN PAIRS, unregistered: 18 pair(s) have fewer than 500 shared escaping sources, all involving models that rarely escape. prereg_escape_rival gated this per pair as KA; this prereg gates only the global index, so they are reported rather than excluded.  KW5 NAMED NO THRESHOLD, which is a defect in this prereg: directions and thresholds are numbers here, and 'if one destination dominates' is an adjective. Arm 1's registered gate is 0.50 and this cohort trips it at 0.8832, so every headline is recomputed with each model's modal destination removed: attribution 9 of 12 (0.75), architecture balanced accuracy 0.9, family lift 0.2013 against tokenizer lift 0.1166. All three verdicts hold under the exclusion. Unregistered; the registered figures above stay primary.  REFUSALS: no p-value; no reassignment of Zamba2's architecture label; no claim that a surviving attribution is a CORPUS result, since corpus now varies but is not controlled; no instance identification; no semantic reading. F187's quantization envelope stands unchanged and 4-bit remains fatal.",
